2026-07-07 10:50:05,270 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: Based on our company context, I propose an architecture that leverages our expertise in Cloud architecture, API integration, Data engineering, and Cybersecurity. 

To integrate with existing systems of information, we can utilize our experience with API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, along with API gateways like Kong or Apigee. We will design APIs to interact with business softwares, civil status, town planning, EDM, and user directories, ensuring seamless data exchange and minimal disruption to existing workflows.

For high availability and fast response times, we can deploy the solution on a cloud provider that we have experience with, such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, which offer robust infrastructure and low latency. Our performance benchmarks indicate that we can achieve a p95 response time of 1800ms, which is close to the required 2 seconds. We will also implement auto-scaling and load balancing to ensure the solution can handle varying workloads.

To guarantee security and integrity of data, we will implement our proven security design patterns, including Zero-trust network architecture, VLAN segmentation, mTLS between services, AES-256 encryption at rest, and TLS 1.3 in transit. We will also utilize secrets management tools like HashiCorp Vault or CyberArk Conjur to protect sensitive data.

Additionally, to address sovereignty constraints, we can host the solution on a SecNumCloud-type infrastructure, which ensures that data is hosted exclusively on European Union territory and is not transferred outside the EU. This aligns with our experience in deploying solutions on SecNumCloud, having completed 3 such deployments in the past.

Our containerisation expertise using Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm will enable us to package and deploy the solution efficiently, while monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack will help us ensure the solution's performance and availability.

Overall, our proposed architecture is designed to meet the client's requirements for integration, availability, security, and sovereignty, while leveraging our existing technology stack and expertise.
